{"name":"Closet Skeletons","hex":"#e1ded9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"closet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small room within a house used to store clothing, food, or other household supplies.","Any private space,  bowers in the open air."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Private.","Closeted, secret (especially with reference to gay people who are in the closet)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/closet"},{"term":"skeletons","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of skeleton","Shameful secrets (pluralia tantum; shortened from skeletons in the cupboard or skeletons in the closet)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of skeleton"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skeletons"}],"entries":[{"title":"Closet","blocks":[{"text":"A closet is an enclosed space, with a door, used for storage, particularly that of clothes. Fitted closets are built into the walls of the house so that they take up no apparent space in the room. Closets are often built under stairs, thereby using awkward space that would otherwise go unused."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Old_Jefferson_Louisiana_2016_-_Coolidge_Street_58.jpg/330px-Old_Jefferson_Louisiana_2016_-_Coolidge_Street_58.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Closet"},{"title":"Skeleton","blocks":[{"text":"A skeleton is the structural frame that supports the body of most animals. There are several types of skeletons, including the exoskeleton, which is a rigid outer shell that holds up an organism's shape; the endoskeleton, a rigid internal frame to which the organs and soft tissues attach; and the hydroskeleton, a flexible internal structure supported by the hydrostatic pressure of body fluids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Horse_and_Man.jpg/330px-H